{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And he took the daughter of Levi.</b> He had separated from her because of Pharaoh's decree, and he took her back and entered into a second marriage with her, and she too reverted to being a young woman. She was 130 years old — for she was born when they came to Egypt between the walls, and 210 years they stayed there, and when they left Moses was eighty years old; if so, when she conceived by him she was 130 — and Scripture calls her 'the daughter of Levi' (cf. Sotah 12, Bava Batra 119, and Shemot Rabbah)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:08.769238093Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}